{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1207237-newbie-with-questions","id":1207237,"title":"Newbie with questions!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-04-15T06:18:57-07:00","id":1207237,"title":"Newbie with questions!","content":"Hi guys, I am (or was, it was a really long time ago) a long time player of the old storyteller games (mainly Werewolf: The Apocalypse), and I was blindstuck to know just this year about this &quot;new WOD&quot;. Our group immediatelly bought the Chronicles of Darkness Corebook, and start trying the system. We're long past playing werewolves or vampires, but have fond memories of the system, so we were trying it in a generic, modern special ops missions kinda of sessions, just to get a grip on the rules, and how combat works (we're also gun nuts, so we do care a lot about combat).<br /> Having said all of it, we really liked the new system - it is fast and lethal, but we're left with some questions, that I hope you guys can help us resolve:<br /> Ps.: I tried to search for those same questions in the forum, but found nothing, so sorry if they were answered here before!<br /> <br /> - Some weapons are listed as having &quot;Attack rolls gain the 9-again quality&quot; - this is for the entire attack roll, or just for damage sake? Let me explain: if Russo shots a thug with a shotgun, rolls 6 dice, getting 1,4,5,6,5 and 9, which is re-rolled, resulting in 7, but the thug rolls for dodge, getting 1 success, Russo hits the thug or not? We interpreted that in those cases, the extra success were just for damage, so the thugs ins unscathed, but, if he insted could not dodge, Russo would do 3 (shotgun) plus 2 (successes) lethal damage;<br /> - Are there rules for minigun in any rulebook or suplement? Yes, I know that it is overkill, but the characters called for backup, and the support chopper was supposed to have one. I changed to a HMG, but it got me curious;<br /> - Defense and firearms attack - we got it the first time: page 88 is unforgiven - &quot;Defense does not apply against Firearms attacks.&quot;, but what about spending a point of Willpower to get +2 defense, does it helps against firearms attacks? And what about page 90, Firearms in Close Combat, which states that the target's Defense score is increased by the attacker's gun's size+1? It don't make sense if page 88 states that defense does not apply against Firearms attacks!<br /> - Also, about Defense, Dodge is statistically worse than common defense, as you're exchanging &quot;automatic success&quot; equals to your defense for a Dice Pool totalling Defense x2, as your standard chance of success in each die is 30%, you, in reallity, are spending an action to actually lower your defenses by 40%! Am I wrong? Are there any modifiers that I am not considering?<br /> <br /> Thanks for your patience, and sorry for the long post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24118-vitorrossi","name":"vitorrossi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T06:38:55-07:00","id":1207241,"title":"","content":"I can't answer any of these with my limited knowledge of the rules, but i can direct you to the Ask a Simple Question, Get a Simple Answer thread for general system and crossover questions. They have a lot of good contributors there. They really need to pin the thread if you ask me.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness/\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...d-of-darkness/</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T07:03:05-07:00","id":1207247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vitorrossi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1207237-newbie-with-questions#post1207237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi guys, I am (or was, it was a really long time ago) a long time player of the old storyteller games (mainly Werewolf: The Apocalypse), and I was blindstuck to know just this year about this &quot;new WOD&quot;. Our group immediatelly bought the Chronicles of Darkness Corebook, and start trying the system. We're long past playing werewolves or vampires, but have fond memories of the system, so we were trying it in a generic, modern special ops missions kinda of sessions, just to get a grip on the rules, and how combat works (we're also gun nuts, so we do care a lot about combat).<br /> Having said all of it, we really liked the new system - it is fast and lethal, but we're left with some questions, that I hope you guys can help us resolve:<br /> Ps.: I tried to search for those same questions in the forum, but found nothing, so sorry if they were answered here before!</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll try to answer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - Some weapons are listed as having &quot;Attack rolls gain the 9-again quality&quot; - this is for the entire attack roll, or just for damage sake? Let me explain: if Russo shots a thug with a shotgun, rolls 6 dice, getting 1,4,5,6,5 and 9, which is re-rolled, resulting in 7, but the thug rolls for dodge, getting 1 success, Russo hits the thug or not? We interpreted that in those cases, the extra success were just for damage, so the thugs ins unscathed, but, if he insted could not dodge, Russo would do 3 (shotgun) plus 2 (successes) lethal damage; </div> </div> </div>9 Again does count against Dodging. Just to clarify a thing: It's 8 to 10 that counts as successes, not 7.<br /> It does make more sense to only apply it to damage since 9 Again in this case is about increasing damage without accuracy, but that's extra bookkeeping that can slow down the game. But you do what is best for your group.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - Are there rules for minigun in any rulebook or suplement? Yes, I know that it is overkill, but the characters called for backup, and the support chopper was supposed to have one. I changed to a HMG, but it got me curious; </div> </div> </div>I think it's in one of the first edition Armory books, but I'm not sure. It's not updated to second edition, though, but that would only require decreasing the weapon modifier by 1.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - Defense and firearms attack - we got it the first time: page 88 is unforgiven - &quot;Defense does not apply against Firearms attacks.&quot;, but what about spending a point of Willpower to get +2 defense, does it helps against firearms attacks? </div> </div> </div>No. It increases your existing Defense, which does not apply against ranged attacks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And what about page 90, Firearms in Close Combat, which states that the target's Defense score is increased by the attacker's gun's size+1? It don't make sense if page 88 states that defense does not apply against Firearms attacks! </div> </div> </div>Point blank is an exception to not applying Defense. If you're in hand-to-hand range you can try to manoeuvre yourself in a way that you can't for ranged attacks (other than just dropping prone). Note that the book only says &quot;ranged&quot; rather than Firearms.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - Also, about Defense, Dodge is statistically worse than common defense, as you're exchanging &quot;automatic success&quot; equals to your defense for a Dice Pool totalling Defense x2, as your standard chance of success in each die is 30%, you, in reallity, are spending an action to actually lower your defenses by 40%! Am I wrong? Are there any modifiers that I am not considering? </div> </div> </div>I think I see the mistake. Defense doesn't remove successes. Defense removes dice from the dice pool before it's rolled.<br /> <br /> 3 Defense reduces the opponent's dice pool by 3, which is on average 1 success. If you instead Dodge and roll 6 dice, you'll get on average 2 successes, and cancel 2 of the opponent's successes. Dodging actually doubles the effectiveness of your Defense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Thanks for your patience, and sorry for the long post. </div> </div> </div>No problem.<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: As a side note I can recommend Hurt Locker. It contains a bunch of optional rules for combat (most notably lingering injuries), and loads of Fighting Style Merits, along with some Supernatural Merits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 04-15-2018, 10:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T15:45:43-07:00","id":1207426,"title":"","content":"Tessie wrapped things up pretty well, so just to add something I observed:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vitorrossi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1207237-newbie-with-questions#post1207237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Some weapons are listed as having &quot;Attack rolls gain the 9-again quality&quot; - this is for the entire attack roll, or just for damage sake? Let me explain: if Russo shots a thug with a shotgun, rolls 6 dice, getting 1,4,5,6,5 and 9, which is re-rolled, resulting in 7, but the thug rolls for dodge, getting 1 success, Russo hits the thug or not? We interpreted that in those cases, the extra success were just for damage, so the thugs ins unscathed, but, if he insted could not dodge, Russo would do 3 (shotgun) plus 2 (successes) lethal damage;</div> </div> </div> </div>9-Again applies to the roll normally, not just being restricted to damage, but in your particular cited example, 9-Again did nothing. 8, 9, and 10 are rolled successes in CofD. 7 isn't.<br /> <br /> This points to two things that can be missed easily in CofD:<br /> 1) 9-Again isn't as useful as it seems at first glance. It never turns an uncontested failed roll into a successful one, and its yield is very limited unless your dice pool is already rather large.<br /> 2) 8 is a high target number to meet, meaning there remain fair odds even a large dice pool will fail. This is why, unlike the older World of Darkness games, CofD doesn't measure gradations of success beyond dramatic failure, regular failure, regular success, and exceptional success. An uncontested roll with even a single rolled success should be treated as a normal success, and not a partial or limited one, because this is not an uncommon result even for skilled specialists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T18:21:59-07:00","id":1207468,"title":"","content":"Fair odds for failure seems a bit of a strong statement. 7 dice is when your odds of failing by not rolling any successes drops below 10%, 9 dice is when you fall below 5%, and 13 dice is when you fall below a 1% chance of failing.<br /> <br /> I mean, what you feel is a high rate of success/failure is kinda subjective, but the numbers above seem some pretty basic benchmarks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T19:01:14-07:00","id":1207477,"title":"","content":"You're right, that might have been a bit strong wording compared to what I meant to emphasize: simply that the dice are swingy such that you generally shouldn't measure &quot;how successful&quot; a typical roll is by the number of rolled successes, just the overall probability that any successes occurred. Attack rolls are the most common exception, but it's important to keep in mind for most non-combat actions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T01:39:44-07:00","id":1207580,"title":"","content":"A &quot;large dice pool&quot; is also highly subjective. For regular mortals fresh out of character creation 7 dice could be their highest dice pool. A major splat who gets to add their maxed power trait to certain rolls twice or three times will have 40+ dice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T13:24:57-07:00","id":1207743,"title":"","content":"Emphases mine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vitorrossi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1207237-newbie-with-questions#post1207237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Some weapons are listed as having &quot;Attack rolls gain the 9-again quality&quot; - this is for the entire attack roll, or just for damage sake? Let me explain: if Russo shots a thug with a shotgun, rolls 6 dice, getting 1,4,5,6,5 and 9, which is re-rolled, resulting in 7, but the thug rolls for dodge, getting 1 success, Russo hits the thug or not? We interpreted that in those cases, the extra success were just for damage, so the thugs ins unscathed, but, if he insted could not dodge, Russo would do 3 (shotgun) plus 2 (successes) lethal damage;</div> </div> </div> </div>This is correct. But I dunno from where you're getting the attack's second success. He'd need to score 2s to dodge entirely, otherwise, with 1s in his dodge he takes 4 instead of 5 damage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vitorrossi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1207237-newbie-with-questions#post1207237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Are there rules for minigun in any rulebook or suplement? Yes, I know that it is overkill, but the characters called for backup, and the support chopper was supposed to have one. I changed to a HMG, but it got me curious;</div> </div> </div> </div>Go with something like Damage 5, 8 again, Init -7, I'm sure you'll be able to figure out short/medium/long ranges on your own. Clearly capable of automatic fire.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vitorrossi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1207237-newbie-with-questions#post1207237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Defense and firearms attack - we got it the first time: page 88 is unforgiv<b>i</b>n<b>g</b> - &quot;Defense does not apply against Firearms attacks.&quot;, but what about spending a point of Willpower to get +2 defense, does it helps against firearms attacks? And what about page 90, Firearms in Close Combat, which states that the target's Defense score is increased by the attacker's gun's size+1? It don't make sense if page 88 states that defense does not apply against Firearms attacks!</div> </div> </div> </div>Defense doesn't applies against firearms (unless you're within brawl distance of the gunner). So you can spend all the WP in the world to try and dodge a sniper shot, but it won't help you unless he's 5 feet away from you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vitorrossi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1207237-newbie-with-questions#post1207237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Also, about Defense, Dodge is statistically worse than common defense, as you're exchanging &quot;automatic success&quot; equals to your defense for a Dice Pool totaling<b>*</b> Defense x2, as your standard chance of success in each die is 30%, you, in reality<b>*</b>, are spending an action to actually lower your defenses by 40%! Am I wrong? Are there any modifiers that I am not considering?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're facing the barrel of a shotgun and the opponent just scored 1s on his attack, you'll take 4 damage. It's safer to dodge, but it's also a gamble. I allow players to declare the dodge post attack, but give the attacker the previously penalized dice back. Easy to roll 2 successes with say, a pool of 8.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","user":"Malus","date":". 04-16-2018, 04:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}